  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="e9d0e60b-1472-57db-bc20-ad494f3f7320" activityNameId="04c18de8-850d-576f-9782-7320616cc530" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Sheet rolling, aluminium</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Sheet rolling, aluminium
Aluminium ingots of 500-700 mm thickness and up to 25 tonnes weight, are rolled, first hot, then cold, to a final sheet thickness ranging from 0.2 to 6 mm. The module can be applied also for section bar rolling of aluminium.;
Synonyms: profile rolling, section bar rolling; 
UUID: 6113497a-792f-38e7-a69a-420dff702898
All the process steps, which can be attributed to semi-fabrication (sawing, scalping, hot rolling, cold rolling, solution heat treatment, finishing and packaging), are included. Does not include the material beeing rolled, only the amount of scrap lost in waste is balanced as primary aluminium input. Includes the transport of the materials to the plant, but does not include the transport of the product to the customer.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Avarage technique for European Union. The infrastructure was assumed to be the same as for rolling steel.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: Literature, estimation for transport and infrastructure 
Extrapolations: see technology and sampling procedure
Uncertainty adjustments: Precision of the data set is referred to be of 5 % by the reference, nevertheless uncertainty was estimated by filling out the uncertainty scoring
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_6113497a-792f-38e7-a69a-420dff702898.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="20a9bf48-6cea-59b4-ad08-000cb981f2d0" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
